From d8711b11ff2451e050789b416b347a00ab14d86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Hutchins <jeff@currentclient.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 10:32:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] fix(android): ringer-mode aware media playback and
 service hardening

Absorbs the Android half of cc-mob-app's
patches/@twilio+voice-react-native-sdk+1.7.0.patch as first-class code:

- Rewrite MediaPlayerManager around Ringtone/MediaPlayer/Vibrator instead
  of SoundPool: incoming ringtone uses STREAM_RING via the Ringtone class
  so ring volume and DND are respected; honors ringer mode
  (silent/vibrate/normal) and the vibrate-when-ringing setting; outgoing
  ringback and disconnect tones use USAGE_VOICE_COMMUNICATION. Only reset
  audio mode when MODE_RINGTONE was active so in-call routing set by
  AudioSwitch is preserved (PRO-3848).
- CallListenerProxy: use startRingback()/playDisconnectTone() APIs.
- VoiceActivityProxy: only add lock-screen window flags for call-related
  intents and drop FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON so the device can sleep after a
  call; use setShowWhenLocked/setTurnScreenOn on O_MR1+.
- VoiceService: handle ACTION_PUSH_APP_TO_FOREGROUND before UUID guards,
  return START_NOT_STICKY instead of crashing when the call UUID or call
  record is missing (GH-430), and keep the incoming ringtone playing in
  foregroundAndDeprioritizeIncomingCallNotification.
- AndroidManifest: add VIBRATE permission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
